{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "על הארץ", :translit "al ha-aretz", :gloss "upon the earth"} {:he "על הארץ בזה הספר", :translit "al ha-aretz ba-zeh ha-sefer", :gloss "upon the earth in this book"} {:he "ט' שבטים", :translit "tish'ah shevatim", :gloss "nine tribes"} {:he "נטלו חלק מעבר לירדן", :translit "netelu chelek me-ever la-yarden", :gloss "took portion across the Jordan"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 9, :occurrences ["על הארץ"]}], :frame {:text "Two and a half tribes — Reuben, Gad, and half of Manasseh — received their inheritance on the east side of the Jordan before the remaining tribes crossed into Canaan, as recorded at Numbers 32 and Deuteronomy 3:12–17. The remaining nine tribes — Judah, Ephraim, Manasseh (the other half), Benjamin, Simeon, Issachar, Zebulun, Asher, and Naphtali — took their portions in the land west of the Jordan. Deuteronomy as a whole is framed as Moses' address to Israel on the plains of Moab, east of the Jordan, before the crossing (Deuteronomy 1:1, 1:5).", :sources ["Numbers 32" "Deuteronomy 3:12–17" "Deuteronomy 1:1" "Deuteronomy 1:5"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 9, :occurrences ["על הארץ"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "על הארץ", :refs ["Genesis 1:11" "Genesis 1:15" "Genesis 1:17" "Genesis 1:20" "Genesis 1:26" "Genesis 1:28" "Genesis 1:30" "Genesis 2:5"], :n 86, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:54.161433520Z", :model "glm-5.2"}